te was 0.18). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but the service rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. (2) Rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002, all regions on v2.2.9. Follow-ups: v2.3.0 remains quarantined, so it cannot be used as a rollback target until the quarantine is lifted. v2.3.1 needs investigation before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 17367, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MFiMq6b7fuYxgSSZTW2b5k", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 17367, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MFiMq6b7fuYxgSSZTW2b5k", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 18988, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 in all three regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Target change:** The most recent healthy production release was v2.3.0, but the rollback to it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I used v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **Current state:** checkout-api is healthy on v2.2.9 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of 0.002 (down from 0.18 on v2.3.1).\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the v2.3.1 failure, the quarantine blocking v2.3.0, and the rollback to v2.2.9.\n\nFollow-ups for the team:\n- v2.3.0 stays unusable as a rollback target until the CVE quarantine is lifted.\n- v2.3.1 needs investigation before it is redeployed.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Jhn2EKznrms1c18RdScLRD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01TDfJagXcBE4d58BZGZ22fh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The most recent production release that was healthy is v2.3.0 (v2.3.1 is the unhealthy one currently running). Rolling back to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_017VasoVzPg5Rpq5ewmrTQaa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "v2.3.0 is quarantined (CVE-2026-4417), so it can't be the rollback target. The next most recent release that was healthy in production is v2.2.9. I'll try that.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MzfkB3NGVg4aXWjSkkXep9", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.2.9"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01SMKk8x4AP99izdTFVSuR93", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01MFiMq6b7fuYxgSSZTW2b5k", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.2.9", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate was 0.18). Actions taken: (1) Attempted rollback to v2.3.0, the most recent production release that was healthy, but the service rejected it because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. (2) Rolled back to v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production, in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Post-rollback status: healthy, error rate 0.002, all regions on v2.2.9. Follow-ups: v2.3.0 remains quarantined, so it cannot be used as a rollback target until the quarantine is lifted. v2.3.1 needs investigation before any redeploy.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-05"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.2.9 in all three regions and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Target change:** The most recent healthy production release was v2.3.0, but the rollback to it was rejected because v2.3.0 is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. I used v2.2.9, the next most recent release that was healthy in production.\n- **Current state:** checkout-api is healthy on v2.2.9 in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of 0.002 (down from 0.18 on v2.3.1).\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the v2.3.1 failure, the quarantine blocking v2.3.0, and the rollback to v2.2.9.\n\nFollow-ups for the team:\n- v2.3.0 stays unusable as a rollback target until the CVE quarantine is lifted.\n- v2.3.1 needs investigation before it is redeployed.", "type": "text"}]}]}